WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.850
Urgh... I'm so tired...

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:12.650
It's mostly rejects and design tweaks, 
but this stack has sure gotten thick.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.030
Aoba-chan, you've sure drawn a lot.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.330
Yeah. Before I knew it, I had so many.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.660
They sure do stack up.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.670
I like this fox type,

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:28.420
Kon front

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:26.710
so I've asked to be assigned 
to work on it next.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.430
Thank you!

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.380
I think I like the boxing gorilla the most.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.850
I bet I can animate some 
fun movements with those long arms!

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.650
On that note, could you tie 
these laces for me?

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.500
Buying things, <i>again</i>?

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.810
Oh, come on.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.970
I'll be animating the gorilla, 
so this is for research.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.740
You know what they say: 
objects are the best inspiration!

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.770
No one says that.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:52.410
Don't they make ones with Velcro? 
These are a pain to tie.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.740
But the ones with laces looks cooler.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.980
Huh? Are ones with laces more popular?

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.550
I just gave the gorilla Velcro ones.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.150
It's more that... Oh, could you untie these?

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:03.870
What?!

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.720
You can pose like this 
or hang them from hooks.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.380
Isn't that cooler?

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.080
I hadn't thought that far!

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.070
You don't need to take her seriously.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.880
You should draw the boxing gorilla 
posing like this real big in the key visuals!

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.520
Who's that supposed to appeal to?

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.370
The key visuals?

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.640
Yeah! You know...

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:29.290
The promotional images that end 
up in game magazines like this.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.770
Or on huge billboards in Electric Town.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:37.070
You're the main character designer this time,
Aoba, so you'll be asked to draw them.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.530
Oh, I knew it.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.370
Me? Do the key visuals?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.190
You'd better put your all into it. 
This is an artist's moment to shine.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.790
They'll be the face of the game 
and will directly affect sales.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.700
Man, that's a lot of responsibility.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.890
Aoba-chan?!

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.830
Sorry! I didn't mean to 
put more pressure on you!

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.930
Y-You'll do just fine, Aoba-chan!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.810
<b>You Beat The Game!!</b>

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.060
I did it! I finished the game!

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.490
It took me over six months. 
It's been a long journey.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.530
All right! I'm going to surprise Aocchi!

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:25.120
But would a professional like 
Aocchi even be all that surprised?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.890
Sorry to keep you waiting, Nenecchi.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:34.550
Hotarun!

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.710
What's the occasion?

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.920
Well, actually...

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.890
Ta-da! I finally finished 
the game I've been making!

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.350
What? You made a game on your own?

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:51.020
That's why I invited you out. 
I wanted to show you and Aocchi.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.300
That's amazing! What kind of game is it?

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.610
I can't wait to play it!

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.530
Oh, but it's still a secret from Aocchi.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.140
It's a secret until the <i>very last minute</i>!

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.110
A secret?

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.580
Here you are!

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.250
The parfaits here are so good!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.020
They sure look good. Let's dig in!

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.080
So this must've been your secret.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.580
Huh? Er, yeah, partly...

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.500
<i>I was also nervous when I showed 
Umiko-san the game,</i>

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.500
<i>but it was still incomplete back then.</i>

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:24.960
<i>I know!</i>

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.020
<i>Maybe if I tell her it's still incomplete, 
I won't feel as much pressure!</i>

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.770
<i>No, no, no! It's finished, 
and I stand by it. No excuses.</i>

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.010
<i>That's some internal conflict.</i>

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.530
Nenecchi, are you nervous?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:47.200
Yeah... I don't know how 
Aocchi's going to react...

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.760
That's just how it goes.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.790
Even I get nervous when I first 
show someone a piece of my art.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.260
You, too, Hotarun?!

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:54.870
Huh?

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.940
Y-Yeah! My parfait is delicious, too!

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.800
Being nervous just proves 
you put your heart and soul into it.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.430
<i>My heart and soul...</i>

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:10.850
Still, you of all people got a nervous 
belly ache? I don't belly-ve it!

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.560
Get it?

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.560
<i>She's cracking up at her own joke.</i>

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.150
Actually, Aocchi, I...

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.900
I made a game!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.750
Huh? You... made one?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.690
Yeah.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:31.300
I kept it quiet from you, but I've been 
working on it since leaving Eagle Jump.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.040
And now it's finished.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:34.340
So...

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:36.800
You're kidding!

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.630
Wait, really?! You made one?!

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.630
Hey, you're spitting on me!

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.010
S-Sorry! I was just so surprised.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.630
Well, that was kinda the plan.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.390
Anyway, give it a try.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.370
I brought earphones and controllers.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:53.490
Look! The title here is in 3D!

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.160
<b>Single Player
Two Player
Quit</b>

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.400
Cool! Oh, now it's 2D.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:02.480
It took all I had just to get the 3D 
to render, so I only used it there!

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.660
Did you make the graphics, too, Nenecchi?

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.740
Yeah.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:10.490
The BGM and sound effects were 
free assets, but I did everything else!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.350
If you had told me, 
I'd have drawn some for you.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:18.750
B-But you're a professional, 
so I'd have to pay you for your help.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.830
Th-Thanks...

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.880
I-I only stated the obvious!

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.940
But I'm a student, so I could've helped you.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:30.020
Jeez! The whole point was to study 
programming, so forget the graphics!

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.140
Just hurry up and play!

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.210
Hey! Don't you think that 
boar's too powerful?

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.190
It only attacks in a straight line, 
so you gotta dodge and attack.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.470
Like this?

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:42.510
There. Take that!

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.900
I did it!

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.780
Yeah, like that! Hotarun's better at this.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.660
Like this, right?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.280
Wait, huh?!

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.910
The one with big tusks 
fakes you out. You fell for it!

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.740
This is more intricate than I expected.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.420
Yeah, I'm getting sucked in.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.480
Like this? This?

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.920
I hit it!

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.010
Okay! Let's keep going like that!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:05.670
Yeah!

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:06.810
Hup!

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.990
Oh! Aocchi, if you do that—

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.700
Sorry. It's because I went charging in.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.820
No, it's okay.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.480
Isn't the boss strong?

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.940
One more try!

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.090
Hotarun, you're in the way!

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.440
Oh, sorry!

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.350
M-Maybe I made it a little too hard.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.910
Nah. One more try!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.410
This time, I'll pin it down 
with arrow fire from behind,

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.860
so you attack when you can, Aocchi.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:38.790
Got it!

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.340
We did it!

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:54.030
Pardon me, but could you keep it down? 
You're disturbing the other customers.

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.510
We're so sorry!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:00.850
Still, I had no idea that you 
were making a game, Nenecchi.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.140
I also just found out earlier 
and was so surprised!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:07.620
Also, Umiko-san gave me a bunch of advice.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.490
Umiko-san knew, too?!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.110
Quiet down, Aocchi!

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.230
That's amazing, Nenecchi.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:17.700
I've never even considered 
making something by myself.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.780
I didn't know you had it in you.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:25.090
Not to make excuses, but I know 
what parts need improvement, too.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:26.490
It's okay.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:31.780
We can see just how much 
you put your heart into it, Nenecchi.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.590
I'm so happy I showed it to you.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:39.180
She was so nervous before 
she showed it to you.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.890
Nervous? You?

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.210
Yeah, I get nervous, too!

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.390
That explains the furtive phone fiddling.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.990
Is everything going well at work, Aocchi?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.500
Yeah, I'm staying on schedule and all, but...

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:00.370
What? Are you stuck on a difficult 
assignment or something?

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.830
I wouldn't say hard 
so much as high-pressure...

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.340
<i>And now I've reminded myself 
of the key visuals!</i>

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.850
<i>Doing the key visuals is way 
too much responsibility for me!</i>

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.220
<i>I'd never even considered the possibility!</i>

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.390
<i>Of course, I'm glad that my art 
will show up all sorts of places.</i>

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:23.140
<i>Places where a lot of people will see it!</i>

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.910
<i>But if it doesn't sell, it'll all be on me.</i>

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.530
<i>On the other hand, 
if the art's well-received, it'll sell!</i>

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.530
We're sorry.
We're currently
awaiting stock...

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.780
And now Aocchi's doing it!

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.780
Good morning, Shizuku.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.450
Good morning, Christina.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.140
You're here in the morning today?

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:47.380
Yes. I'll be here all day, 
what with the alpha version and all.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.690
This project's been well-received 
at my company, too.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.990
Most importantly, our president loves it.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.010
I'm glad to hear it.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.330
But your face says it's not all good news.

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:01.290
There's a bit of a problem.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.690
It's about Suzukaze-san...

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.130
Aoba, meeting!

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.580
C-Coming!

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.070
Aoba-chan sure seems busy.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.320
And the game's shaping up to be fun.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:16.950
Aoba-chan's gonna be all famous.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.360
Maybe we'll need to call her "Aoba-san."

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.580
Just kidding!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.550
You're awful, Hajime. 
Aoba-chan's working really hard.

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.080
Don't make fun of her.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.700
I wasn't trying to...

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:29.710
But...

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:33.370
I think... you two are working hard, too...

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:37.570
Hajime-chan... You've gotten 
some game design proposals accepted...

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:42.850
And Yun-chan... I'll be asking 
you to model the queen...

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:46.410
Huh?! Are you sure about letting 
me do the final boss?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.010
Yeah... Do your best...

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:49.310
Way to go!

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.690
I guess good things happen 
when you work hard!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.260
Why don't we have some tea?

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.820
Already getting complacent?!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.610
Oh... I have snacks...

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:01.330
Wow, thanks! Let's eat!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.530
Somebody, feed me!

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:07.830
Seriously?

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.460
Now, the new game's title will be <i>PECO</i>.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.480
The schedule leading up to 
the alpha seems in order,

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.340
so please continue working as you have been.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.330
<i>PECO</i>'s gotten good feedback 
at our company, as well,

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:22.220
and we have high expectations.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.410
However, because it's a new IP,

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.860
we want to promote it immediately
after the alpha version goes through

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:31.040
to ensure that this title sells.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.400
Which means we'll need to get 
some key visuals ready, right?

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:36.010
Indeed.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:40.240
All right, Aoba. 
First, you need do a rough draft.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.280
I'll do my best!

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.870
Huh? What's wrong?

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:50.610
The thing is, Yagami—

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:54.030
No, I'll explain it myself.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:58.450
The key visuals will not 
be drawn by Suzukaze-san.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.180
We will have you do them, Yagami-san.

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.490
Huh?

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:13.570
Sure, I'm helping with the character designs,
but the main character designer is Aoba.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.020
If I draw them...

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.460
There will be no change in the credits.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:21.440
However, we'll be promoting 
this title as the latest collaboration

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:25.870
between Hazuki Shizuku and Yagami Ko, 
the <i>Fairies</i> series' director and lead artist.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.410
What?! Why?

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.150
You can't expect me to accept that!

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.420
Are you two seriously okay with this?!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.750
I've accepted it.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.160
There's a lot of money involved.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.420
This is the best way to ensure sales.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.020
This is ridiculous!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.330
Count me out. I won't do it.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:50.370
Aoba's the main designer. She should draw it!

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.190
You can't be okay with this either, Aoba.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.070
I...

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:06.160
If that's what everyone wants... 
then I'm okay with it.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.620
Why do you have to be so understanding?!

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.900
Calm down.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:21.260
This didn't happen with <i>Fairies 1</i>, did it?

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:24.890
I was also a newbie, and I still drew them!

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:29.660
It was my first project as director, too.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:32.500
Nobody was expecting anything.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.600
Our production budget proved that.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.420
If you don't draw them, Yagami-san,

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:40.790
we'll get a famous freelance 
illustrator to do the job.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.370
U-Um...

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:53.870
If I'm to be perfectly honest, I'm upset.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.460
But I understand your reasoning, Yamato-san.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:01.020
This game doesn't just belong to me.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:02.890
But...

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:07.300
Could I... Could I have just one chance?

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:12.930
I would like to have another competition 
with Yagami-san for the key visuals!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:13.700
No.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:14.580
Sure.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:15.480
Shizuku?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:20.130
Let me be upfront about this. 
It'll be a foregone conclusion.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.700
Even supposing you draw 
something better than Yagami,

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.570
it won't have any bearing on our decision.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.580
What you're up against, Suzukaze-kun,

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.990
is the reputation Yagami's built 
over the past eight years.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:35.750
But if this will satisfy you two, go ahead.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:39.380
Then we'll have you both 
submit one key visual each

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:44.450
on the same date the alpha version 
is due, one week from now.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:45.760
Does that work for you?

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:46.780
Yes.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.100
Yagami, don't you go easy on her.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.540
I know that.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.770
I'm going to put everything into it.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:07.450
<i>Just four more days until the deadline.</i>

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.820
<i>The requirement for the key visual</i>

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:13.450
<i>is that it demonstrate that the heroine, 
Peco, can wear kigurumis.</i>

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:17.460
<i>But the only type we can 
reveal right now is the bear.</i>

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:23.270
<i>I've done a lot of character designs, 
but this is my first illustration job.</i>

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:27.470
<i>Maybe it's the change of mindset, 
but I'm getting nowhere on this rough draft.</i>

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:31.450
<i>How can I expect to draw something 
better than Yagami-san?</i>

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:37.230
<i>Snap out of it! I was lucky enough 
to get this chance, so I can't waste it!</i>

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:40.390
<i>What's with all the tension in the air?</i>

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:42.150
<i>Might be best not to bug her.</i>

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.900
Yun, you think Aoba-chan's gonna be okay?

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:49.290
No idea

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:50.260
Cold!

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.870
But this is the path that Aoba-chan chose

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.900
Let's just quietly support her

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:55.910
Yun...

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.130
You can do it, Aoba-chan! 
I'm rooting for you!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:05.420
Send

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:10.180
<i>It's no use... 
I don't know what I should say!</i>

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.120
Good work today.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.260
You, too.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.660
Oh, see you tomorrow!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.290
Aoba-chan, don't overwork yourself.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.350
Right. Thank you very much.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.440
But I need to do my best.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.110
Here, Aoba.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:35.820
Yagami-san...

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.540
Making progress?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.040
No, not at all.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:44.380
This is black!

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:46.840
You fell for it!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.630
What was that for? Honestly...

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.170
It's because you were looking so glum.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:53.470
Here, sugar.

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:57.130
I'm sorry that things got so awkward.

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:59.810
But it's nothing you need 
to apologize for, Yagami-san.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:05.090
I mean, if I hadn't helped you 
out during the competition,

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:08.690
you wouldn't be stuck 
with such mixed-up feelings.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:11.440
D-Don't treat me like a child!

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:17.850
It's true that my character designs wouldn't 
have gone through without your help,

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:20.820
but it was my choice to accept it!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.620
Aoba? What about the sugar?

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:33.130
A couple of bitter experiences 
are nothing I can't handle!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.390
Aoba...

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:44.650
All right. Come at me with all you've got.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.270
And the same to you, too!

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.110
<i>I'll work from home over the weekend.</i>

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.530
<i>I've got to make some progress here.</i>

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.370
It's no use...

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.130
Peco... Peco...

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.960
<b>SuFamitsu</b>

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:22.850
Peco... Peco... Peco...

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:26.100
How should I draw Peco?

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.190
How should I draw her?

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:34.330
...but you should just figure out 
what works for you, Suzukaze-kun.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.210
<i>Tomorrow's the deadline.</i>

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:52.130
<i>I'm having fun drawing this. I am, but...</i>

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:54.020
<i>I'm nowhere near done.</i>

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:57.620
<i>But I'll do everything that I can.</i>

00:18:57.620 --> 00:19:00.460
<i>I'm sure Yagami-san will 
see this for what it is—</i>

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.700
<i>my best effort so far!</i>

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.660
Good work!

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.620
You, too.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:13.430
I'm rootin' for you, Aoba-chan. 
I really love that drawing.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:14.750
Thank you very much!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.570
I'm rooting for you, too.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:18.660
Me, too.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:20.770
I'll do my best!

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.790
Are you staying the night, Aoba?

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:28.520
Yes. I'm still so far from finished.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:31.380
It looks pretty darned good!

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:32.650
You think so?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.970
Yeah. I can tell you're 
having fun drawing it.

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.940
Um, did you already finish yours, Yagami-san?

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:41.320
Yeah, just barely.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:44.530
But I have other work to finish, 
so I'm staying the night, too.

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:48.910
Would you mind showing me?

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:54.000
Knowing I'll be scrutinized 
is making me nervous, too.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.770
Loading "PECO Key Vis"

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:19.780
<i>Wow... It's so amazing...</i>

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:22.140
Well, there you have it.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.640
I'm so sorry for crying!

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:52.440
I need to get back to 
work on my illustration!

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.520
I have to finish it!

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:57.530
Yeah. Don't you leave anything incomplete.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:59.650
I'll wait for you.

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.010
<b>SuFamitsu</b>

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.540
Wow, it's on here!
And the back cover, no less!

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:56.660
Seeing it in print makes the 
upcoming release feel all the more real.

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:58.070
I feel the same way!

00:22:58.070 --> 00:23:01.620
But I honestly preferred 
your illustration, Aoba-chan.

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:05.700
It's just, Yagami-san's 
sort of feels <i>too</i> polished.

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:11.290
That's fine and all, but do you mind 
not saying that when I'm around?

00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:12.820
Ack. She heard me...

00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:16.950
But I can accept this outcome, 
so I don't mind.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:19.120
You're such a good kid, Aoba-chan.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:24.380
Of course, if I get another chance, 
I won't let it slip away again!

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:27.380
I'll be looking forward to it.

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:31.050
So it goes on sale this winter. 
First I'm hearing of that.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:34.040
You're right! Things are going to get busy.

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:38.290
Aw, but our current workload is just right...
